            <ArticleTitle>Preliminary results of a soft novel lumbar intervertebral prothesis (DIAM) in the degenerative spinal pathology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a series of 43 patients suffering from lower limb pain, almost constantly associated with chronic or acute backpain, treated by microsurgical nerve root decompression and by implantation of a soft intervertebral prothesis (DIAM). Satisfying results were obtained in 97% of cases, inducing the authors to consider the device a reliable tool for curing low-back pain and sciatica. Selection criteria are exposed and discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
